WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.381
Module 16 is about deployment and staying current.

2
00:00:02.381 --> 00:00:07.000
First: how the app updates itself, and how it proves an update is trustworthy before applying it.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.182
The app checks for updates on startup, automatically, no action needed.

4
00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:17.000
If one's found you'll see it — otherwise it stays out of your way.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.809
Want to check right now instead of waiting for the next launch?

6
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:25.321
Settings, Data and updates, Check for updates.

7
00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:27.000
Same check, on demand.

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.925
What matters most here: updates are signed.

9
00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:31.612
Before anything is applied, the app verifies that signature.

10
00:00:31.612 --> 00:00:38.015
If the check fails — a corrupted download, a tampered file, anything that doesn't match — the update is refused outright, not silently applied.

11
00:00:38.015 --> 00:00:39.000
Fail closed, not open.

12
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Why bother signing at all?

13
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.077
Because an update replaces the app's own binary — the one thing on your machine that's implicitly trusted.

14
00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.423
A silent bad update would be the worst possible failure mode.

15
00:00:46.423 --> 00:00:49.962
Signing turns “trust the download” into “trust the download only if it proves who it's from.

16
00:00:49.962 --> 00:00:50.000
”

17
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.234
Updates keep the app current.

18
00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:56.000
Next: what happens when you're done with it — the uninstall path, and exactly what does and doesn't get removed.

